\[\cos (2A - B) = \sin (A + B) = 1.\]Since $A + B = 180^\circ,$ $0 < A + B < 180^\circ.$  Then we must have
\[A + B = 90^\circ.\]This means $A < 90^\circ$ and $B < 90^\circ,$ so $2A - B < 180^\circ$ and $2A - B > -90^\circ.$  Hence,
