& & & & & \stackrel{4}{4} & \stackrel{}{5}_6 \\
& & & \times & & 5 & 0_6 \\
\cline{4-7} & & & 4 & 0 & 1 & 0_6 \\
\end{array}$$Now, we divide by $2$ to obtain that the answer is $\boxed{2003}_6$. $$
\begin{array}{c|cccc}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{2} & 0 & 0 & 3 \\
